statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ, let τ : Fin n → ℝ^P be orthonormal, and let w ∈ NVector (Eucl P) n satisfy w = simpleNVector τ or w = −simpleNVector τ. Here simpleNVector τ = τ_1 ∧ ⋯ ∧ τ_n is the functional b ↦ b(τ_1, …, τ_n). Then:
(i) |w(b)| ≤ ‖b‖ for every n-covector b ∈ Covector (Eucl P) n, where ‖b‖ is the operator norm of the continuous alternating map b;
(ii) w ≠ 0.
